---@field endOffset? string Filter results to objects whose names are lexicographically before endOffset. If startOffset is also set, the objects listed will have names between startOffset (inclusive) and endOffset (exclusive).
---@field includeTrailingDelimiter? boolean If true, objects that end in exactly one instance of delimiter will have their metadata included in items in addition to prefixes.
---@field maxResults? number Maximum number of items plus prefixes to return in a single page of responses. As duplicate prefixes are omitted, fewer total results may be returned than requested. The service will use this parameter or 1,000 items, whichever is smaller.
---@field pageToken? string A previously-returned page token representing part of the larger set of results to view.
---@field prefix? string Filter results to objects whose names begin with this prefix.
---@field projection? gcp.storage_v1.ListObjectsProjectionEnum|string Set of properties to return. Defaults to noAcl.
---@field startOffset? string Filter results to objects whose names are lexicographically equal to or after startOffset. If endOffset is also set, the objects listed will have names between startOffset (inclusive) and endOffset (exclusive).
---@field userProject? string The project to be billed for this request. Required for Requester Pays buckets.
---@field versions? boolean If true, lists all versions of an object as distinct results. The default is false. For more information, see [Object Versioning](https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/object-versioning).
---@field matchGlob? string Filter results to objects and prefixes that match this glob pattern.
---@field filter? string Filter the returned objects. Currently only supported for the contexts field. If delimiter is set, the returned prefixes are exempt from this filter.
---@field softDeleted? boolean If true, only soft-deleted object versions will be listed. The default is false. For more information, see [Soft Delete](https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/soft-delete).
---@field includeFoldersAsPrefixes? boolean Only applicable if delimiter is set to '/'. If true, will also include folders and managed folders (besides objects) in the returned prefixes.

