---@field ipFilter? gcp.storage_v1.BucketIpFilter The bucket's IP filter configuration. Specifies the network sources that are allowed to access the operations on the bucket, as well as its underlying objects. Only enforced when the mode is set to 'Enabled'.
---@field kind? string The kind of item this is. For buckets, this is always storage#bucket.
---@field labels? gcp.storage_v1.StringMap User-provided labels, in key/value pairs.
---@field lifecycle? gcp.storage_v1.BucketLifecycle The bucket's lifecycle configuration. See [Lifecycle Management](https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/lifecycle) for more information.
---@field autoclass? gcp.storage_v1.BucketAutoclass The bucket's Autoclass configuration.
---@field location? string The location of the bucket. Object data for objects in the bucket resides in physical storage within this region. Defaults to US. See the [Developer's Guide](https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/locations) for the authoritative list.
---@field locationType? string The type of the bucket location.
---@field logging? gcp.storage_v1.BucketLogging The bucket's logging configuration, which defines the destination bucket and optional name prefix for the current bucket's logs.
---@field generation? string The generation of this bucket.
---@field metageneration? string The metadata generation of this bucket.
---@field name? string The name of the bucket.
---@field owner? gcp.storage_v1.BucketOwner The owner of the bucket. This is always the project team's owner group.
---@field projectNumber? string The project number of the project the bucket belongs to.
---@field retentionPolicy? gcp.storage_v1.BucketRetentionPolicy The bucket's retention policy. The retention policy enforces a minimum retention time for all objects contained in the bucket, based on their creation time. Any attempt to overwrite or delete objects younger than the retention period will result in a PERMISSION_DENIED error. An unlocked retention policy can be modified or removed from the bucket via a storage.buckets.update operation. A locked retention policy cannot be removed or shortened in duration for the lifetime of the bucket. Attempting to remove or decrease period of a locked retention policy will result in a PERMISSION_DENIED error.
---@field objectRetention? gcp.storage_v1.BucketObjectRetention The bucket's object retention config.
---@field rpo? string The Recovery Point Objective (RPO) of this bucket. Set to ASYNC_TURBO to turn on Turbo Replication on a bucket.
---@field selfLink? string The URI of this bucket.
---@field softDeletePolicy? gcp.storage_v1.BucketSoftDeletePolicy The bucket's soft delete policy, which defines the period of time that soft-deleted objects will be retained, and cannot be permanently deleted.
---@field storageClass? string The bucket's default storage class, used whenever no storageClass is specified for a newly-created object. This defines how objects in the bucket are stored and determines the SLA and the cost of storage. Values include MULTI_REGIONAL, REGIONAL, STANDARD, NEARLINE, COLDLINE, ARCHIVE, and DURABLE_REDUCED_AVAILABILITY. If this value is not specified when the bucket is created, it will default to STANDARD. For more information, see [Storage Classes](https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/storage-classes).
---@field timeCreated? string The creation time of the bucket in RFC 3339 format.
---@field updated? string The modification time of the bucket in RFC 3339 format.
---@field softDeleteTime? string The soft delete time of the bucket in RFC 3339 format.
---@field hardDeleteTime? string The hard delete time of the bucket in RFC 3339 format.
---@field versioning? gcp.storage_v1.BucketVersioning The bucket's versioning configuration.
---@field website? gcp.storage_v1.BucketWebsite The bucket's website configuration, controlling how the service behaves when accessing bucket contents as a web site. See the [Static Website Examples](https://cloud.google.com/storage/docs/static-website) for more information.
---@field satisfiesPZS? boolean Reserved for future use.
---@field satisfiesPZI? boolean Reserved for future use.
---@field bucket string Name of a bucket.
---@field ifMetagenerationMatch? string Makes the return of the bucket metadata conditional on whether the bucket's current metageneration matches the given value.
---@field ifMetagenerationNotMatch? string Makes the return of the bucket metadata conditional on whether the bucket's current metageneration does not match the given value.
---@field predefinedAcl? gcp.storage_v1.PatchBucketsPredefinedAclEnum|string Apply a predefined set of access controls to this bucket.
---@field predefinedDefaultObjectAcl? gcp.storage_v1.PatchBucketsPredefinedDefaultObjectAclEnum|string Apply a predefined set of default object access controls to this bucket.
---@field projection? gcp.storage_v1.PatchBucketsProjectionEnum|string Set of properties to return. Defaults to full.
